    "proof_chain": "For clause (i) 01HK and 0H7H give the necessary stalk surjection; 01T1 permits the finite denominator argument through 00CR and 00CP; 01IG and 01IO package the resulting quotient-spectrum chart. For clause (ii) 01HE and 0H7H give the necessary stalk isomorphism; D000320 first applies 01TX and only then 0BX6 to realize the inverse stalk map and compare both composites after shrinking.",
    "root_source_disposition": "Both equivalences are exact derived composites of existing Stacks results. No genuinely nonduplicative theorem was proved necessary; no root TeX theorem, PDF, visual artifact, issue, registry mutation, or canon correction is warranted."
  },
  "residual_guards": [
    {
      "id": "R000804",
      "guard": "Preserve the composite route and do not invent a single omnibus official tag."
    },
    {
      "id": "R000805",
      "guard": "Preserve EGA's source-point neighbourhood quantifier rather than asserting a global immersion or isomorphism."
    },
    {
      "id": "R000806",
      "guard": "Finite type is essential in clause (i) because infinitely many algebra generators need not clear on one principal neighbourhood."
    },
    {
      "id": "R000807",
      "guard": "Finite type alone does not satisfy 0BX6 item (2a); use local Noetherianity through 01TX to obtain finite presentation."
    },
    {
      "id": "R000808",
      "guard": "Reuse D000320 S001196-S001205 for EGA's literal §6.5.1 citation and both inverse-composite comparisons."
    },
    {
      "id": "R000809",
      "guard": "Retain the explicit affine denominator argument through 01T1 00CR 00CP and 01IG without claiming a nonexistent single target theorem."
    }
  ],
